"Let $H$ be a finite group, and let $\\mathcal{M}$ be any minor-closed class of $H$-gain-graphic matroids. A **gain-graphic matroid** is a frame matroid obtained from a graph whose edges are assigned elements of $H$. **Finite-group gain-graphic excluded-minor conjecture.** The class $\\mathcal{M}$ has only finitely many excluded minors, and can hence be defined in monadic second-order logic. This is an analogue for gain-graphic matroids of the finite-field finiteness phenomenon for excluded minors and logical definability."